From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] vulkan: add pl_vulkan_create_headless_swapchain

Adds a public swapchain backend for embedding the libplacebo render
pipeline into presentation systems that don't expose a VkSurfaceKHR —
e.g. AVSampleBufferDisplayLayer + IOSurface on Apple platforms,
DMA-buf + a Wayland sub-surface, or a server-side render-to-disk
pipeline. The user owns the VkImage pool; libplacebo wraps each image
into a `pl_tex` once at creation time and hands them out via
acquire/present callbacks on every frame.

Mirrors the structure of `vulkan/swapchain.c` (the surface-backed
implementation), with the surface dance excised: there is no
VkSurfaceKHR, no vkAcquireNextImageKHR, no vkQueuePresentKHR. The
synchronisation contract is the same as a surface swapchain — the
caller of `pl_swapchain_submit_frame` receives a binary VkSemaphore
which signals when the GPU finishes writing, and is responsible for
making the foreign API (Metal, Wayland, etc.) wait on it before
reading.

Layout transitions: `VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_UNDEFINED` on acquire (image is
producer-owned and free, prior contents discarded);
`VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_GENERAL` + `VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_EXTERNAL` on submit (the
foreign API takes ownership; GENERAL is the only Vulkan layout
guaranteed compatible with all subsequent uses, which matches Metal /
DMA-buf consumption semantics).
